# Resolved by `op run` for the one-time X OAuth 2.0 authorisation, which is
# only needed if the vault holds no console-generated Access Token and
# Secret (`./tools/x.py check` says). Committed on purpose: every op:// below
# is a REFERENCE, not a value.
#
#   op run --env-file=tools/x-auth.env -- ./tools/x.py auth
#
# Only the app: the step that mints the refresh token cannot also depend on
# it (op run refuses to start when a reference does not resolve). For `auth`
# the item has to hold the OAuth 2.0 Client ID and Client Secret of the app
# `podcast-engine` in the X Developer Console, a confidential client (type
# "Web App, Automated App or Bot"). Everything that uses the token afterwards
# resolves tools/x.env.
X_APP_ID=op://Engineering/X podcast app/username
X_APP_SECRET=op://Engineering/X podcast app/credential
